    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0806" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v10p1/pg772"/>

                <head>312. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Consulate General in Nicosia<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d312-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-02-25T18:35:00-05:00">February 25, 1959,
                            6:35 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>341. Contel 375.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d312-f2"/> In replying queries regarding
                    future of US communication facilities in Cyprus
                    you should avoid giving Cypriots grounds for belief question will be open for
                    discussion between new Government of Cyprus and USG. You should seek to avoid
                    comment but, if pressed, you may reply to such queries by saying USG expects
                    provision for continuity of US facilities will be
                    worked out in context detailed agreement which will give effect to documents
                    signed in London.</p>
                <p>FYI. We propose shortly to follow up on
                    suggestion final para London 4378.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d312-f3"/> End FYI.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d312-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d312-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 511.47C2/2–2459. Confidential;
                    Priority. Drafted by Blood. Repeated to
                    London, Athens, and Ankara.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f2" n="1" xml:id="d312-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 375 from Nicosia, February 24, requested guidance concerning a request
                    by a representative of Reuters News Agency for a statement about the future of
                    U.S. communications facilities on Cyprus. (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Ibid</hi>.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f3" n="2" xml:id="d312-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 4378 from London, February 20, reported Foreign Office assurances that
                    they had safeguarded U.S. interests in the agreement signed on February 19 and
                    that these rights would extend to all agreements signed prior to the end of
                    British administration in Cyprus. The final paragraph reported that the Foreign
                    Office suggested consultations between the United States and United Kingdom over
                    communications facilities prior to talks with Greece, Cyprus, and Turkey. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>., 747C.00/2–2059)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
